The table structure information is (table names): 
['sqlite_sequence', 'Player_Attributes', 'Player', 'Match', 'League', 'Country', 'Team', 'Team_Attributes']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  
(Mentioned only once – they apply to every query that follows)

• Match."season": season we are analysing.  
• Match."league_id": connects each match to its league (→ League table).  
• Match."country_id": sometimes handy, but league already stores country‑id.  
• Match."home_team_api_id", Match."away_team_api_id": who played.  
• Match."home_team_goal", Match."away_team_goal": basis for result → points.  
• Team."team_api_id", Team."team_long_name": to show a readable team name.  
• League."id", League."name", League."country_id": league info.  
• Country."id", Country."name": country info.  

Basic conditions that will frequently appear  

• home win  : Match."home_team_goal"  > Match."away_team_goal"  
• away win  : Match."away_team_goal"  > Match."home_team_goal"  
• draw     : Match."home_team_goal" = Match."away_team_goal"  

Below are ten exploratory SQL statements (simple → complex → final result).  
All are restricted to 20 rows only so they run quickly while we explore.  

```sql
-- 1. List every different season that exists in the dataset
SELECT DISTINCT "season"
FROM "Match"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. List every country that has at least one league in the DB
SELECT DISTINCT "name"
FROM "Country"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. List every league name (with the id so we can join later)
SELECT DISTINCT "id", "name"
FROM "League"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Show a few team long names together with their team_api_id
SELECT DISTINCT "team_api_id", "team_long_name"
FROM "Team"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Grab a sample of matches: who played, score, league and season
SELECT  "Match"."season",
        "League"."name"   AS "league",
        "Match"."home_team_api_id",
        "Match"."away_team_api_id",
        "Match"."home_team_goal",
        "Match"."away_team_goal"
FROM "Match"
JOIN "League" ON "League"."id" = "Match"."league_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Convert one side of each match (home team) into points earned
SELECT "season",
       "match_api_id",
       "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
       CASE
         WHEN "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal" THEN 3
         WHEN "home_team_goal" = "away_team_goal" THEN 1
         ELSE 0
       END AS "points"
FROM "Match"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Convert both teams of each match into points (home + away) via UNION ALL
SELECT "season", "league_id", "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
       CASE
         WHEN "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal" THEN 3
         WHEN "home_team_goal" = "away_team_goal" THEN 1
         ELSE 0
       END AS "points"
FROM "Match"
UNION ALL
SELECT "season", "league_id", "away_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
       CASE
         WHEN "away_team_goal" > "home_team_goal" THEN 3
         WHEN "home_team_goal" = "away_team_goal" THEN 1
         ELSE 0
       END
FROM "Match"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Aggregate the previous query: total points per team, per season, per league
WITH match_points AS (
    SELECT "season", "league_id", "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
           CASE
             WHEN "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal" THEN 3
             WHEN "home_team_goal" = "away_team_goal" THEN 1
             ELSE 0
           END AS "points"
    FROM "Match"
    UNION ALL
    SELECT "season", "league_id", "away_team_api_id",
           CASE
             WHEN "away_team_goal" > "home_team_goal" THEN 3
             WHEN "home_team_goal" = "away_team_goal" THEN 1
             ELSE 0
           END
    FROM "Match"
)
SELECT "season", "league_id", "team_api_id", SUM("points") AS "total_points"
FROM match_points
GROUP BY "season", "league_id", "team_api_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Identify, for every season‑league combo, the maximum point tally
WITH match_points AS (
    SELECT "season", "league_id", "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
           CASE
             WHEN "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal" THEN 3
             WHEN "home_team_goal" = "away_team_goal" THEN 1
             ELSE 0
           END AS "points"
    FROM "Match"
    UNION ALL
    SELECT "season", "league_id", "away_team_api_id",
           CASE
             WHEN "away_team_goal" > "home_team_goal" THEN 3
             WHEN "home_team_goal" = "away_team_goal" THEN 1
             ELSE 0
           END
    FROM "Match"
), team_season_points AS (
    SELECT "season", "league_id", "team_api_id",
           SUM("points") AS "total_points"
    FROM match_points
    GROUP BY "season", "league_id", "team_api_id"
)
SELECT "season", "league_id", MAX("total_points") AS "max_points"
FROM team_season_points
GROUP BY "season", "league_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query: Champion for every season (20 rows sample) with team, league & country
WITH match_points AS (
    SELECT "season", "league_id", "home_team_api_id" AS "team_api_id",
           CASE
             WHEN "home_team_goal" > "away_team_goal" THEN 3
             WHEN "home_team_goal" = "away_team_goal" THEN 1
             ELSE 0
           END AS "points"
    FROM "Match"
    UNION ALL
    SELECT "season", "league_id", "away_team_api_id",
           CASE
             WHEN "away_team_goal" > "home_team_goal" THEN 3
             WHEN "home_team_goal" = "away_team_goal" THEN 1
             ELSE 0
           END
    FROM "Match"
), team_season_points AS (
    SELECT "season", "league_id", "team_api_id",
           SUM("points") AS "total_points"
    FROM match_points
    GROUP BY "season", "league_id", "team_api_id"
), champions AS (
    SELECT tsp.*
    FROM team_season_points AS tsp
    JOIN (
        SELECT "season", "league_id",
               MAX("total_points") AS "max_points"
        FROM team_season_points
        GROUP BY "season", "league_id"
    ) AS mx
      ON tsp."season"      = mx."season"
     AND tsp."league_id"   = mx."league_id"
     AND tsp."total_points"= mx."max_points"
)
SELECT   "Country"."name"      AS "country",
         "League"."name"       AS "league",
         "Team"."team_long_name" AS "champion_team",
         champions."season",
         champions."total_points"
FROM champions
JOIN "League"  ON "League"."id"        = champions."league_id"
JOIN "Country" ON "Country"."id"       = "League"."country_id"
JOIN "Team"    ON "Team"."team_api_id" = champions."team_api_id"
ORDER BY champions."season", "league"
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten progressively build an understanding of the data and culminate in a query that produces (sampled) season champions together with their league, country, and total points.
